    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After more than two years of formal investigation into competitive practices, European authorities have finalized their assessment and are expected to issue a significant antitrust fine before the August recess. The core finding, under the bloc's digital markets framework, is that the search service operator consistently prioritized proprietary services in its search results, effectively self-preferencing against affected market participants. This anticipated regulatory ruling will impose a substantial financial sanction, adding to a decade-long history of competition enforcement against the parent company.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "why-1",
